included government formation charges and professional fees and expenses in connection with the preparation of the Fund&rsquo;s offering
documents and its basic organizational and contractual documents. The Fund bears, either directly or by reimbursing the Manager, all
expenses in connection with the ongoing offer and sale of Interests.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Under
U.S. generally accepted accounting principles, organization costs and start-up costs are expensed as incurred. However, the Fund intends
to depart from U.S. GAAP, by electing to treat these costs as deferred expenses and to amortize them over a period of not less than 60
months beginning with the month in which the partnership begins business.</FONT></P>

